From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:02:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allocate AFC memory in dynamic path

Firmware can request an AFC buffer when PCIe target memory is allocated
through the DMA API. The dynamic allocator currently rejects that type,
although the fixed-memory allocator supports it.

Handle AFC requests with the existing dynamic chunk allocator and retain
the same AFC_MEM_SIZE bound used by the fixed PCIe allocation path.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -3007,6 +3007,15 @@
 		 * allocate memory, assigns NULL and FW will handle this without crashing.
 		 */
 		switch (chunk->type) {
+		case AFC_REGION_TYPE:
+			if (chunk->size > AFC_MEM_SIZE) {
+				ath12k_err(ab,
+					   "AFC memory request size %u exceeds limit %u\n",
+					   chunk->size, AFC_MEM_SIZE);
+				ret = -EINVAL;
+				goto err;
+			}
+			fallthrough;
 		case HOST_DDR_REGION_TYPE:
 		case M3_DUMP_REGION_TYPE:
 		case PAGEABLE_MEM_REGION_TYPE:
